# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
N8N_HOST=https://your-n8n.example.com

# Sync (pull / push / watch / status / publish / unpublish) and the MCP guard
# (mcp connect / mcp serve) ride n8n's MCP server. Preferred auth: OAuth — run
# `n8n-decanter init` once; it opens n8n's consent page and stores rotating
# credentials in a gitignored .decanter-auth.json. No token in this file.
# Headless/CI alternative: a bearer token minted in n8n → Settings → MCP →
# API key (takes precedence over the OAuth file when set):
#N8N_MCP_TOKEN=...

# OPTIONAL public API key — only for the surfaces MCP cannot serve
# (executions, data-table reads, and backup). Prefer a SCOPED key (n8n →
# Settings → n8n API → Create) limited to what the tool actually uses, not a
# full-access key — smaller blast radius if .env leaks:
#   workflow:list                                         (init's connection check)
#   execution:read  execution:list                        (executions)
#   dataTable:list  dataTable:read                        (data-tables — only
#   dataTableColumn:read  dataTableRow:read                while "dataTables" is on)
#   workflow:read  workflow:create                        (backup create/restore)
# A full-access key also works.
#N8N_API_KEY=n8n_api_...

# OPTIONAL auth mode — set this when a proxy in front of n8n attaches the n8n credentials itself (a 
# gateway, an auth sidecar). decanter then sends NO credential header at all: no Authorization on MCP, 
# no X-N8N-API-KEY on REST, and N8N_API_KEY above stops being required — the proxy's key needs the 
# scopes listed above instead.
#
# A placeholder value in N8N_API_KEY is NOT a workaround: a proxy that adds its own key APPENDS it to 
# the one the client sent, and n8n answers 401 to the pair. Only omitting the header works, which is 
# what this does.
#
# Any value other than "upstream" or "credentials" (the default) is an error on every verb, offline 
# ones included — a typo must not silently put the header back. `n8n-decanter init . --host 
# <proxy-url> --auth upstream` writes it for you.
#N8N_DECANTER_AUTH=upstream
